# Image to WebP

**Skill:** `.cursor/skills/image-to-webp/SKILL.md` (MUST Read and follow when this rule loads).

## Scope

- MUST apply when the agent adds or updates a **shipping** `.png`, `.heic`, or `.heif`, or leaves a shipping path pointing at those extensions.
- MUST NOT auto-convert under `tmp/`, `node_modules/`, `.git/`, `vendor/`, or other clearly vendored / scratch trees unless the user points at a file there.
- MUST NOT treat intermediate build scratch (for example a temp PNG before encode) as a shipping asset.

## When a shipping raster appears

- MUST convert each in-scope raster to `.webp` before finishing the task, unless the user explicitly asks to keep the source format.
- MUST follow skill `image-to-webp` for tool checks, install-ask (and install only after user agreement), `cwebp` encode, reference updates, and source removal.
- MUST NOT silently keep PNG/HEIC/HEIF because `cwebp` or a HEIC decoder is missing.
- Host products MAY override the convert command with a product CLI (documented in a host skill) while still obeying WebP output, ref updates, and no silent keep-source-format.
- MAY leave existing `.jpg`, `.jpeg`, and `.webp` unchanged unless the user asks to recompress or convert those too.

## Verify

- MUST run the project's documented build or check (for example `make build`, `hugo`, or the nearest test that loads the asset) after path changes so broken references surface immediately.
